  "prompt": "# Adversarial code review \u2014 Offband caplog framed download (#396)\n\nAdversarial embedded C++ review for **Offband** (MeshCore LoRa firmware companion, nRF52 +\nESP32). Find bugs; don't praise. This adds the framed **download-to-app** for the serial-capture\nbuffer, on top of the merged sink (#393) + CLI (#395).\n\nDesign context (assume true):\n- The companion protocol sends frames to the app via `_serial->writeFrame()`. The send queue is\n  4-deep and **drops when full** (#169), so large responses MUST be streamed **one frame per\n  idle main-loop pass** from a drain function called in `checkSerialInterface()` while\n  `!isWriteBusy()` \u2014 never a synchronous burst. Existing precedents: `blockListDrain`,\n  `offbandStreamDrain`.\n- Fork-private companion command codes use the `0xC0+` range. This adds `CMD_OFFBAND_CAPLOG =\n  0xC3` and reply frames `[0xC3, sub, \u2026]` with sub-codes START(0x01)/CHUNK(0x02)/END(0x03).\n- Contract: request `0xC3` \u2192 `START[total_len 4B LE]` \u2192 `CHUNK[bytes]*` \u2192 `END`. Client\n  reassembles \u2192 file.\n- On download start, capture is **auto-stopped** (`meshLogSetEnabled(false)`) to freeze the ring\n  so the offset-based chunk stream is stable. `meshLogSnapshot(out, cap, offset)` returns 0 when\n  `offset >= bytesUsed()`.\n- `out_frame` / `cmd_frame` are `MAX_FRAME_SIZE+1` byte buffers; `MAX_FRAME_SIZE` = 176.\n\nVerified: builds on RAK4631 companion (nRF52) + Ebyte EoRa-S3 companion (ESP32); the offset\nsnapshot has native unit tests.\n\nReview concretely (cite file:line, rank by severity):\n\n1. **Frame protocol correctness.** START byte layout (4-byte LE total), CHUNK sizing\n   (`MAX_FRAME_SIZE - 2` payload into an `MAX_FRAME_SIZE+1` buffer), END. Any buffer overrun,\n   wrong length passed to `writeFrame`, or endianness/spec mismatch a client would choke on?\n2. **Drain / queue-safety.** Is the one-frame-per-idle-pass integration correct? Can the stream\n   stall, never send END, double-send END, or busy-loop? Interaction with the other drains\n   (block-list, contacts, config) \u2014 can two stream at once or clobber `out_frame`?\n3. **State lifecycle.** `_caplog_streaming`/`_caplog_off` init in the constructor; reset + END\n   terminator on APP_START (re)connect. Any path that leaves a stale stream, sends END twice, or\n   starts a new download while one is in flight?\n4. **Auto-stop semantics.** Freezing capture on START \u2014 correct choice? Any race between the\n   START snapshot of `bytesUsed()` and the drain reads? What if the buffer is empty (total 0)?\n5. **Anything missed** \u2014 a security/DoS angle (remote triggering downloads), a simpler approach,\n   or a correctness gap.\n\nBe terse. If fine, say so.\n\n=== C:\\Users\\stryc\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Dev-meshcore-firmware\\ce5045af-5978-4a55-8b3c-9ce0975d4fe7\\scratchpad\\396-diff.txt ===\ndiff --git a/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.cpp b/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.cpp\nindex e12b69cf..17e65917 100644\n--- a/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.cpp\n+++ b/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.cpp\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@\n \n #include <Arduino.h> // needed for PlatformIO\n #include <Mesh.h>\n+#include <MeshLog.h>  // #396: serial-capture buffer access for the caplog download\n \n // Offband fork-only companion-API frame codes (config 0xC0 / GPS 0xC1 / block 0xC2)\n // + shared enums. Self-contained (only <stdint.h>); included unconditionally so the\n@@ -103,6 +104,14 @@ namespace offband { MqttBrokerPool& wifiObserverPool(); }\n // pair is companion-available (no observer gate) and is never submitted upstream.\n #define CMD_OFFBAND_GPS               0xC1  // request: GPS status query\n #define RESP_CODE_OFFBAND_GPS         0xC1  // reply: ASCII \"enabled=.. detected=.. fix=.. lat=.. ...\"\n+// #396: Offband fork-only serial-capture download (companion-only, never on the\n+// mesh). Request 0xC3 -> reply START[total 4B LE] -> CHUNK* -> END, streamed one\n+// frame per idle main-loop pass (F8 #169 queue-safe). Sub-code in reply byte[1].\n+#define CMD_OFFBAND_CAPLOG            0xC3  // request: download the serial-capture buffer\n+#define RESP_CODE_OFFBAND_CAPLOG      0xC3  // reply: [0xC3, sub, ...]\n+#define CAPLOG_SUB_START              0x01  // [0xC3,0x01, total_len(4B LE)]\n+#define CAPLOG_SUB_CHUNK              0x02  // [0xC3,0x02, <up to MAX_FRAME_SIZE-2 bytes>]\n+#define CAPLOG_SUB_END                0x03  // [0xC3,0x03]\n \n // Stats sub-types for CMD_GET_STATS\n #define STATS_TYPE_CORE               0\n@@ -1002,6 +1011,8 @@ MyMesh::MyMesh(mesh::Radio &radio, mesh::RNG &rng, mesh::RTCClock &rtc, SimpleMe\n   _ob_stream = OB_STREAM_NONE;   // F8 (#169): no config-response stream in flight\n #endif\n   _blk_listing = false;   // #241: no block-LIST stream in flight\n+  _caplog_streaming = false;  // #396: no caplog download in flight\n+  _caplog_off = 0;\n   offline_queue_len = 0;\n   app_target_ver = 0;\n   clearPendingReqs();\n@@ -1422,6 +1433,23 @@ void MyMesh::handleCmdFrame(size_t len) {\n     _serial->writeFrame(out_frame, 1 + strlen(txt) + 1);  // +1: NUL-terminated (Offband convention)\n     return;\n   }\n+  // #396: serial-capture download (companion-only). Freeze the ring (auto-stop\n+  // capture) so the offset stream is stable, send START with the total byte\n+  // count, then stream CHUNK* -> END one frame per idle pass via caplogDrain().\n+  if (cmd_frame[0] == CMD_OFFBAND_CAPLOG) {\n+    meshLogSetEnabled(false);                       // freeze for a clean download\n+    uint32_t total = (uint32_t)meshLogBytesUsed();\n+    out_frame[0] = RESP_CODE_OFFBAND_CAPLOG;\n+    out_frame[1] = CAPLOG_SUB_START;\n+    out_frame[2] = (uint8_t)(total & 0xFF);\n+    out_frame[3] = (uint8_t)((total >> 8) & 0xFF);\n+    out_frame[4] = (uint8_t)((total >> 16) & 0xFF);\n+    out_frame[5] = (uint8_t)((total >> 24) & 0xFF);\n+    _serial->writeFrame(out_frame, 6);\n+    _caplog_off = 0;\n+    _caplog_streaming = true;\n+    return;\n+  }\n   // #241: block-list sync (companion-API only; NEVER on the mesh). 0xC2.\n   // Receive-side store maintenance: ADD/REMOVE/CLEAR are single-frame acks;\n   // LIST streams (START -> one key/frame -> END) via blockListDrain so it never\n@@ -1555,6 +1583,12 @@ void MyMesh::handleCmdFrame(size_t len) {\n       _blk_listing = false;\n       MESH_DEBUG_PRINTLN(\"APP_START mid-stream: sent block-LIST END terminator (#241)\");\n     }\n+    if (_caplog_streaming) {  // #396: terminate an in-flight caplog download for the (re)connecting client\n+      uint8_t h[2] = { RESP_CODE_OFFBAND_CAPLOG, CAPLOG_SUB_END };\n+      _serial->writeFrame(h, 2);\n+      _caplog_streaming = false;\n+      MESH_DEBUG_PRINTLN(\"APP_START mid-stream: sent caplog END terminator (#396)\");\n+    }\n #ifdef OFFBAND_OBSERVER\n     if (_ob_stream == OB_STREAM_VIEW) {\n       uint8_t h[2] = { offband::RESP_CODE_OFFBAND_CONFIG, offband::OCFG_R_VIEW_END };\n@@ -2619,6 +2653,26 @@ void MyMesh::blockListDrain() {\n   _blk_list_i++;\n }\n \n+// #396: emit ONE chunk frame of an in-flight caplog download. Called from\n+// checkSerialInterface once per idle main-loop pass while !isWriteBusy(), so the\n+// companion send queue (drops-when-full, #169) drains between frames instead of\n+// being flooded. The ring is frozen (capture auto-stopped at START), so the\n+// offset stream is stable. Snapshot returning 0 signals the buffer is exhausted.\n+void MyMesh::caplogDrain() {\n+  const size_t cap = (size_t)MAX_FRAME_SIZE - 2;   // [0]=code, [1]=sub-code\n+  out_frame[0] = RESP_CODE_OFFBAND_CAPLOG;\n+  size_t n = meshLogSnapshot(&out_frame[2], cap, _caplog_off);\n+  if (n == 0) {                                    // buffer exhausted -> END\n+    out_frame[1] = CAPLOG_SUB_END;\n+    _serial->writeFrame(out_frame, 2);\n+    _caplog_streaming = false;\n+    return;\n+  }\n+  out_frame[1] = CAPLOG_SUB_CHUNK;\n+  _serial->writeFrame(out_frame, 2 + n);\n+  _caplog_off += n;\n+}\n+\n void MyMesh::enterCLIRescue() {\n   _cli_rescue = true;\n   cli_command[0] = 0;\n@@ -2809,6 +2863,9 @@ void MyMesh::checkSerialInterface() {\n   } else if (_blk_listing                 // #241: drain an in-flight 0xC2 block-LIST,\n              && !_serial->isWriteBusy()) {  // one key frame per idle pass (queue-safe)\n     blockListDrain();\n+  } else if (_caplog_streaming            // #396: drain an in-flight 0xC3 caplog download,\n+             && !_serial->isWriteBusy()) {  // one chunk frame per idle pass (queue-safe)\n+    caplogDrain();\n   } else if (_iter_started              // check if our ContactsIterator is 'running'\n              && !_serial->isWriteBusy() // don't spam the Serial Interface too quickly!\n   ) {\ndiff --git a/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.h b/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.h\nindex 83ae7bd0..b1f34d97 100644\n--- a/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.h\n+++ b/examples/companion_radio/MyMesh.h\n@@ -251,6 +251,7 @@ private:\n   void loadBlocks();\n   void saveBlocks();\n   void blockListDrain();   // emit one key frame of an in-flight 0xC2 LIST\n+  void caplogDrain();      // #396: emit one chunk frame of an in-flight 0xC3 caplog download\n \n   DataStore* _store;\n   BlockStore _blocks;   // #241: blocked pubkeys (in-memory; persisted via load/saveBlocks)\n@@ -292,6 +293,11 @@ private:\n   // #169). Framing: START=[..,0xFF,count] -> [..,idx,key]* -> END=[..,0xFE].\n   bool    _blk_listing;\n   uint8_t _blk_list_i;\n+  // #396: in-flight serial-capture (caplog) download. Capture is frozen (auto-\n+  // stopped) at START so the ring is stable; caplogDrain() streams one CHUNK\n+  // frame per idle pass from _caplog_off until the buffer is exhausted.\n+  bool    _caplog_streaming;\n+  size_t  _caplog_off;\n   uint8_t app_target_ver;\n   uint8_t *sign_data;\n   uint32_t sign_data_len;\ndiff --git a/src/MeshLog.cpp b/src/MeshLog.cpp\nindex 330a13a9..7b4b29a4 100644\n--- a/src/MeshLog.cpp\n+++ b/src/MeshLog.cpp\n@@ -71,9 +71,9 @@ size_t meshLogBytesUsed() {\n   return n;\n }\n \n-size_t meshLogSnapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap) {\n+size_t meshLogSnapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap, size_t offset) {\n   MLOG_ENTER();\n-  size_t n = g_ring.snapshot(out, out_cap);\n+  size_t n = g_ring.snapshot(out, out_cap, offset);\n   MLOG_EXIT();\n   return n;\n }\ndiff --git a/src/MeshLog.h b/src/MeshLog.h\nindex 6656b9ab..6d4d50b7 100644\n--- a/src/MeshLog.h\n+++ b/src/MeshLog.h\n@@ -57,8 +57,10 @@ uint8_t meshLogGetLevel();\n void   meshLogClear();\n size_t meshLogBytesUsed();\n size_t meshLogCapacity();\n-// Copy up to out_cap captured bytes, oldest-first, into out (for #396 download).\n-size_t meshLogSnapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap);\n+// Copy up to out_cap captured bytes, oldest-first, into out, starting `offset`\n+// bytes in \u2014 lets the #396 download stream the buffer in chunks. Returns bytes\n+// copied (0 when offset >= bytesUsed()).\n+size_t meshLogSnapshot(uint8_t* out, size_t out_cap, size_t offset = 0);\n // Stream the captured buffer to Serial in chunks (local-console `caplog dump`).\n // Best-effort: stop capture first for a clean dump. Framed remote download is #396.\n void   meshLogDumpSerial();\n\n\n",
  "response": "Here is an adversarial code review of the provided diff.\n\n### High Severity\n\n1.  **Logging permanently disabled after one download.**\n    -   `MyMesh.cpp:1429`: On download start, `meshLogSetEnabled(false)` is called to freeze the buffer. However, the log is never re-enabled upon successful completion (`caplogDrain` when `n == 0`) or upon termination via `APP_START` (`MyMesh.cpp:1560-1565`). This permanently disables a core diagnostic feature after a single use, which also presents a denial-of-service vector. The original state of the logger should be saved and restored.\n\n2.  **Concurrent stream protocol corruption.**\n    -   `MyMesh.cpp:1428`: The handler for `CMD_OFFBAND_CAPLOG` unconditionally starts a new stream by setting `_caplog_streaming = true`. It does not check for or terminate other in-flight streams like the block-list (`_blk_listing`).\n    -   `MyMesh.cpp:2815`: The `else if` chain prioritizes `_blk_listing` over `_caplog_streaming`.\n    -   **Impact:** A client can request a caplog download while a block-list is streaming. The client will receive `CAPLOG_START`, then a series of unrelated `BLOCK_LIST` frames, and only then the `CAPLOG_CHUNK`s. This is a severe protocol violation that will break the client parser. New stream requests must be mutually exclusive, either by rejecting the new request or by terminating the old stream.\n\n### Medium Severity\n\n1.  **In-flight download can be restarted, violating protocol.**\n    -   `MyMesh.cpp:1428`: If a `CMD_OFFBAND_CAPLOG` request is received while a caplog download is already in progress (`_caplog_streaming == true`), the handler doesn't reject it. Instead, it resets `_caplog_off = 0` and sends a new `START` frame. The client will receive a `START` frame mid-stream, which is unexpected and will break reassembly logic. The handler should ignore new download requests while one is active.\n\n### Low Severity\n\n1.  **END frame sent for empty log before START.**\n    -   `MyMesh.cpp:2646`: If the log is empty (`meshLogBytesUsed() == 0`), `caplogDrain` will be called once. `meshLogSnapshot` will return `n=0`, causing an `END` frame to be sent immediately. This is correct. However, because the `START` frame is sent synchronously from `handleCmdFrame` and the `END` frame is sent asynchronously from the main loop, it is likely the client receives the `START` frame first. This is fine. (Self-correction: Initial thought was a race, but `writeFrame` is queued, so order is preserved. This point is likely fine, but worth double-checking serial queue behavior under load).\n\n2.  **Potentially breaking API change.**\n    -   `MeshLog.h:62`: The signature of `meshLogSnapshot` is changed. The addition of a default argument makes it source-compatible but not ABI-compatible. If this function is used elsewhere in code that is not recompiled, it will lead to a crash. Given the context, this is likely safe, but it is a fragile change.\n\n3.  **Buffer exhaustion logic in `caplogDrain` is fragile.**\n    -   `MyMesh.cpp:2646`: The stream terminates when `meshLogSnapshot` returns 0. The contract says this happens when `offset >= bytesUsed()`. If `bytesUsed()` is an exact multiple of the chunk size (`MAX_FRAME_SIZE - 2`), the last successful read will make `_caplog_off == bytesUsed()`. The next call to `caplogDrain` will correctly see `n=0` and send `END`. This seems correct, but relies heavily on the precise behavior of `meshLogSnapshot`, which is not part of this diff."
